      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Find the Models for Downlaod - Follow the Download Steps",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "🎙️ REQUIRED CUSTOM NODE: OMNIVOICE TTS\n\nIf this Node shows up red, you need to install the suite manually:\n1. Open your Ubuntu terminal\n2. Navigate to your custom_nodes directory:\n   cd ~/ComfyUI/custom_nodes\n3. Clone the official repository:\n   git clone https://github.com/Saganaki22/ComfyUI-OmniVoice-TTS.git\n4. Install dependencies inside your active venv:\n   cd ComfyUI-OmniVoice-TTS && python install.py\n\n⚠️ 8GB VRAM PASCAL SAFETY TRACK:\nTo completely prevent a CUDA Out-of-Memory (OOM) error on our Tesla P4 / GTX 1080 during the 780-frame render, make sure to set:\n--> keep_model_loaded = False \n\nThis forces PyTorch to instantly purge the 2GB bfloat16 voice model from the VRAM right after the audio generation is complete, freeing up 100% of the graphics memory for the upcoming Float Advanced diffusion pass.\n\n\nI use ComfyUI-IndexTTS2 to save the wav files, you can download it via ComfyUI_Manager search for: ComfyUI-IndexTTS2 or via Github-Repo: https://github.com/snicolast/ComfyUI-IndexTTS2.git\n"
      ],
      "color": "#223",
      "bgcolor": "#335"
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
